      "writtenOn": "2022-08-02T15:45:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like that this uses less data and doesn\u0027t have to define a new appender for DrawWriter (if we can do path chopping on the GPU, the other awkward appender, DynamicInstances could go away too).\n\nBut it\u0027s a bummer that it doesn\u0027t come out as a win, but I have some thoughts below about how we could make that up, which I think are worth playing around a bit. Other RenderSteps are going to need similar decisions about instances and transforms, so I think the data could be generally useful. It also maybe will lead us to the decision that instances aren\u0027t worth it until we can use SSBOs to upload the transform data and the instances become quite small without those 9 floats that are mostly the same for an entire subrun.",
      "revId": "45064a2b09975ad1b945a97c58f7c226ae256c79",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
